1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:06,000
Hi, I’m Athos. I work where design, communication,
and practical AI workflows meet.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:12,000
For this challenge, I built SiteCheck with IBM Bob:
a focused review loop for small websites.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:17,000
It gives people evidence
they can actually act on.

4
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:27,000
This demo has three intentional problems:
missing alt text, a missing label, and a broken link.

5
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:36,800
SiteCheck turns each problem into a finding with an ID,
severity, location, evidence, and recommendation.

6
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:43,000
The important part is the recheck.
I chose the missing form label first.

7
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:50,000
It affects how a user understands the field,
and the correction is easy to verify.

8
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:57,000
After the change, I run the same checks again:
one verified fix and two findings still open.

9
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:00,700
There are zero new regressions,
and the project has forty-two passing tests.

10
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:09,500
IBM Bob helped me plan and implement the Python workflow
across three documented sessions.

11
00:01:09,500 --> 00:01:18,000
I kept product scope, prioritization, code review,
and art direction under human control.

12
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:24,500
That review caught a state-handling issue
that could have hidden a new regression.

13
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:30,600
{\an8\pos(960,132)}Find a problem, decide what matters,
fix it, and prove the result.
